{title: Glory to His name}
{key: G}
{x_theme: blood, cross, salvation}
{x_source: docx:5. Imported/Glory to His name.docx}

{comment: Chorus}
[C]         [G]                [D7]Glory to His Name, Glory to His Name: [G]                       [C]    [G]
There to my heart was the blood applied;     [D7]    [G]
Glory to His Name!

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]Down at the cross where my S[C]avior [G]died,                              [D]
Down where for cleansing from sin I cried, [G]                       [C]    [G]
There to my heart was the blood applied;     [D7]    [G]
Glory to His Name!

{comment: Verse 2}
[G]I am so wondrously s[C]aved from [G]sin,                  [D]
Jesus so sweetly abides within, [G]                        [C]    [G]
There at the cross where He took me in;     [D7]    [G]
Glory to His Name!

{comment: Verse 3}
[G]Oh, precious fountain that s[C]aves from [G]sin,                           [D]
I am so glad I have entered in;[G]                       [C]      [G]
There Jesus saves me and keeps me clean;     [D7]    [G]
Glory to His Name!

{comment: Verse 4}
[G]Come to this fountain so [C]rich and s[G]weet,                            [D]
Cast thy poor soul at the Savior’s feet;[G]                     [C]    [G]
Plunge in today, and be made complete;     [D7]    [G]
Glory to His Name!
